https://github.com/owendswang/ps5-web-file-manager


Vendored source: third_party/
-----------------------------

libsmb2 — SMB2/3 client
  Vendored:  third_party/libsmb2/{lib,include}
  Licence:   LGPL-2.1-or-later
  Texts:     third_party/libsmb2/LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt, third_party/libsmb2/COPYING
  Upstream:  https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2
  MODIFIED:  locally patched. The vendored copy carries a fix for a
             use-after-free in opendir()'s error path (upstream's
             dir->free_cb_data ownership flag plus a cross-file
             smb2_dir_take_cb_data() helper, declared in
             include/libsmb2-private.h). The library's own sources and licence
             are otherwise unchanged.
  Note:      upstream splits this repository by licence; only the LGPL-2.1+
             library directories are vendored. The BSD-licensed examples/ tree
             is NOT included.

libnfs — NFSv3/v4 client
  Vendored:  third_party/libnfs/{lib,include,mount,nfs,nfs4,nlm,nsm,portmap,rquota}
  Licence:   LGPL-2.1-or-later (library sources and include directories), and
             Simplified BSD for the protocol definitions and the files generated
             from them — the */libnfs-raw-<protocol>.[ch] pairs.
  Texts:     third_party/libnfs/LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt, third_party/libnfs/LICENCE-BSD.txt
  Upstream:  https://github.com/sahlberg/libnfs
  Note:      upstream splits this repository by licence; the GPL-3.0
             examples/ tree is NOT vendored, so no GPL-3-only code is pulled in
             beyond what this project already carries as a whole.


Linked but not vendored
-----------------------
libmicrohttpd — embedded HTTP server
  Provided by the PS5 payload SDK as a static library and linked, not vendored.
  Licence:   LGPL-2.1-or-later
  Upstream:  https://www.gnu.org/software/libmicrohttpd/
  Because it is linked statically, distributing binaries carries the usual LGPL
  obligations (notably: the ability to relink against a modified libmicrohttpd).


Referenced, not distributed
---------------------------
The following are separate programs or projects this one interoperates with or
was informed by. No code from them is built into this binary except where noted
above.

  ps5-payload-dev/websrv     GPL-3.0+   HTTP server structure, asset embedding, PKG install
  ps5-payload-dev/ftpsrv     GPL-3.0+   payload conventions, home-screen install flow
  ps5-payload-dev/sdk        GPL-3.0+   build foundation
  seregonwar/zftpd           MIT        socket buffer tuning reference
  itsPLK/ps5-payload-manager GPL-3.0    payload packaging reference
  etaHEN/etaHEN              GPL-3.0    ShellUI URI navigation used before exit
  owendswang/wfm-7zip-helper GPL-3.0    archive extraction, distributed separately
                                        and required at runtime for extraction
                                        and for /api/extract


Licence compatibility
---------------------
The whole is GPL-3.0-or-later. The vendored libraries are LGPL-2.1-or-later,
which the LGPL permits to be combined with GPL-3.0 code (LGPL-2.1 section 3
allows relicensing to GPL-2.0-or-later, and GPL-3.0 is permitted by this
project's own "or later" option). The BSD-licensed rpcgen-derived libnfs files
are permissive and impose no additional condition beyond attribution.

